  "history_of_present_illness": "The patient has a long history of obesity, hypertension (since 1967) and type 2 diabetes (since 1980) leading to progressive diabetic nephropathy. Chronic kidney disease advanced from stage 1 in 1992 to stage 4 by 1999, now awaiting transplantation. Proteinuria and microalbuminuria have been documented. Cardiovascular disease manifested as ischemic heart disease with abnormal cardiac imaging in 1991 and required coronary artery bypass grafting the same year. The patient also has anemia, hypertriglyceridemia, metabolic syndrome, hyperglycemia, and ongoing stress with limited social support. Current management includes insulin, metformin, lisinopril, metoprolol, simvastatin, and nitroglycerin, but several guideline\u2011directed therapies (antiplatelet agents, phosphate binders, ESA) are absent. Recent laboratory values are missing; the recorded A1c of 2.9% is likely erroneous.",
